control: At the end of a unit of work a rotated credential is written back by compare-and-set on the stored bytes the record knew, and an unchanged one is not
removes: the end writes back the token the unit began with under the bytes the record now holds, so a unit begun before an adoption puts its credential back over the operator's
packages: ./process/connections
tests: TestAnEndAfterAnAdoptionLeavesTheOperatorsCredential
scheduled-count: no
integration: yes

